\[
T=2\pi\sqrt{\frac{(1.5\times10^{11})^3}{(6.67\times10^{-11})(2.0\times10^{30})}}
=3.2\times10^7\,\mathrm{s}
\]
This is about one year.

The semi-major axis of the elliptical orbit is
\[
a=\frac{r_p+r_a}{2}
=\frac{1.0\times10^{11}+3.0\times10^{11}}{2}
=2.0\times10^{11}\,\mathrm{m}
\]
For the same star,
\[
T\propto a^{3/2}
\]
so compared with the circular orbit of radius \(1.0\times10^{11}\,\mathrm{m}\),
\[
\frac{T_{\mathrm{ellipse}}}{T_{\mathrm{circle}}}
=\left(\frac{2.0\times10^{11}}{1.0\times10^{11}}\right)^{3/2}
=2^{3/2}=2.83
\]
